<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 98,671 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 98,671 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 98,671 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday, compared to 62,466 tonnes on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Thursday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			24,073	    17,579</p>
<p>    Import cargo			74,598	    23,404</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, five ships are expected to sail and eight to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to</p>
<p>unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Phosphate	     29,887	 Leoanta Glory	due</p>
<p>Palm oil		40,000	 Miraj		  21/3</p>
<p>General Cargo	 3,500	  Wind Seno	    22/3</p>
<p>General Cargo	 3,800	  Arafat		 22/3</p>
<p>Sulphur		 3,101	  Senyar		 22/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
